venv/
.venv/
.env
.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# Telethon session files — contain auth credentials, never commit
*.session
memecoin/data/tg_session
memecoin/data/tg_session.session

# Large raw data file (re-fetchable)
data/historical_raw.json

# watchdog runtime state -- SQLite DB + lock file, never committed.
# NOT a blanket ignore of logs/watchdog/ -- that also caught
# logs/watchdog/audits/ and layer2_heartbeat.json, which Layer 2's
# GitHub Actions workflow explicitly needs to commit (found live: the
# very first real workflow run's "Commit audit artifacts" step failed
# outright with "paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files").
logs/watchdog/state.db
logs/watchdog/state.db-*
logs/watchdog/runner.lock

# Keep logs in repo so GitHub Actions can commit daily results
!logs/market_journal.csv
!logs/live_scan_results.csv
!logs/memecoin_live_journal.csv
!logs/memecoin_social_journal.csv
!logs/memecoin_journal.csv
!logs/exit_route_attempts.csv
!logs/gate_blocks.csv
!logs/trade_telemetry_summary.csv

# V8-REWIRE VR22: files confirmed to be pure operational/scratch state --
# genuinely untracked and NOT previously gitignored, meaning `git stash
# -u` (used during routine deploys when the live process has dirtied a
# tracked file) could legitimately sweep them up as "untracked, not
# ignored" content. logs/v8_funnel.jsonl is the confirmed case: lost
# ~900 historical events this session via exactly this mechanism (see
# docs/RECEIPTS.md's V8-TWIN-FIX section) -- accepted as fine at the time
# because the real research data lives in Supabase, not this file, but it
# should never be able to happen again by accident.
#
# Deliberately NOT included here despite also being untracked: logs/
# price_paths/, logs/research_paths/, logs/signal_candidates.csv, logs/
# winners_journal.csv, logs/t10_velocity.csv, research/data/, research/
# spool/*.jsonl, memecoin/data/memecoin_v8_positions.json,
# memecoin/data/screening_outcomes.csv, logs/memecoin_v8_journal.csv --
# checked against the code that produces/consumes them
# (research/analysis/path_stats.py, replay_exits.py, replay_spool.py,
# tools/analyze_winners.py) and these are real research/backtesting/
# retry-queue data, not scratch. Ignoring them would have been actively
# harmful to the exact freeze-gate work this project depends on. Left
# untracked-but-not-ignored for now -- whether any of these should be
# git-tracked long-term (rather than living VPS-disk-only) is a separate,
# bigger decision this batch doesn't make unilaterally.
logs/v8_funnel.jsonl
logs/watchdog/v8_rewire_deploy_ts.txt
*.log

# V8-FD Phase 1.5 (P15-6): logs/research_paths/ was deliberately left
# untracked-but-NOT-ignored in the VR22 pass above, reasoning it was
# "real research data" -- but that conflated two separate questions.
# Gitignoring a path does not delete it or make it less usable (it lives
# on VPS disk, read by research/analysis/*.py directly, never via git
# history) -- it only protects it from git-native destructive operations
# (git stash -u, git clean) the same way VR22 already protected
# logs/v8_funnel.jsonl for the identical reason. This directory holds
# per-token trade-path CSVs (research/peak_tracker.py) that full-strategy
# EV directly depends on (FD14/FD15) -- exactly the kind of untracked,
# not-ignored, high-value data that has already been silently lost once
# this session (see the RECEIPTS git-stash-u data-loss entries). Whether
# any of it should ALSO be git-tracked long-term remains the separate,
# bigger decision VR22 deferred -- this only closes the stash-safety gap.
logs/research_paths/
